From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:14:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: brcmfmac: Add BCM4350 PCIe ID

The iPad Air 2 (J81) has a BCM4350 Wi-Fi module on PCIe, described by
its PCI compatible pci14e4,43a3 so the endpoint node can carry its
vdd-supply and device-wake-gpios. Add it to the list of PCIe IDs.

Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml      | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
index cb99194e5..000060f30 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ properties:
           - const: brcm,bcm4329-fmac
       - enum:
           - brcm,bcm4329-fmac
+          - pci14e4,43a3  # BCM4350
           - pci14e4,43dc  # BCM4355
           - pci14e4,4464  # BCM4364
           - pci14e4,4488  # BCM4377
